# Docker build-context excludes.
#
# Anything listed here is NOT sent to the Docker daemon, so it is not picked up
# by `COPY . /home/scripts/`. This keeps the runtime image small and the build
# deterministic. It does not change build behaviour: every path the build/runtime
# actually needs is kept.
#
# Intentionally NOT excluded (the build/runtime depend on them):
#   Dockerfile          — the build runs `RUN rm Dockerfile`, which needs it present
#   nginx/              — runtime scripts copy from /home/scripts/nginx/
#   fail2ban/           — `COPY ./fail2ban/fail2ban.local` reads it
#   js/ (except below)  — application source + package manifests

# Version control & local tooling metadata
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.dockerignore
.claude

# Unrelated reference project (Apache image used only for analysis)
apache-with-certificate/

# Design / discussion transcripts (markdown, not part of the product)
initial-chat.md
second-chat.md

# Usage examples — documentation only, never used at build or runtime
examples/

# Test sources and coverage artifacts — never executed inside the image
js/tests/
coverage/

# Dependencies: the runtime node_modules is produced by the builder stage
# (`npm ci --omit=dev`) and copied via `COPY --from=node-builder`. Excluding any
# host-side node_modules stops it from overwriting that clean, prod-only copy.
**/node_modules/

# Dev-only helper script (release notes generation)
generate-release-notes.sh

# OS / editor / log cruft
.DS_Store
*.log
*.swp
